{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1471085-more-than-7-points-in-flaws","id":1471085,"title":"More than 7 points in Flaws?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-12-22T06:50:23-08:00","id":1471085,"title":"More than 7 points in Flaws?","content":"There is some manual, supplement or else - <b><i>nothing homebrew</i></b> - that allows a character to get more than 7 points in flaws?<br /> <br /> And, is it possible to take additional flaws without getting free points, if one chooses to? Because some Flaws can actually be useful, in peculiar circumstances.<br /> Or just cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","name":"Solomon Draak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-22T08:46:56-08:00","id":1471089,"title":"","content":"1. No.<br /> 2. RAW - no. Run it by your GM. I'd usually allow it, there's no real reason not to. If someone wants to take two 4 point flaws - what's the harm?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-22T09:28:59-08:00","id":1471090,"title":"","content":"I thought there was a rule that lets you take excessive flaws without gaining extra points (v20?) <br /> <br /> Players taking flaws because they're &quot;actually useful&quot; aren't thinking enough about them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-22T09:48:59-08:00","id":1471091,"title":"","content":"In some circumstances they can be useful.<br /> <br /> Being Monstrous will kill your social interations... but will scare some opponents.<br /> An Infectious Bite is bad for the Masquerade... but good for dealing with hunters, mages, mabye even Garou and ghouls.<br /> Same as above for Disease Carrier.<br /> Short Fuse means you're probably no good for Elysium... but frenzy can be a blessing in a fight.<br /> Cast No Reflection is bad if you try to pass for human... but good for stealth ( no reflective surfaces betraying you while you sneak upon an opponent or victim ).<br /> Tough of Frost, beside making unpleasant grapple with you, may allow you to run just a little faster in a forest ( plants withering away from you ).<br /> Hands of Hades is that up to 11.<br /> Beacon of the Unholy is good for intimidation, too.<br /> Same as above for Devil's Mark.<br /> Kiss of Death is very exploitable. Sure , the zombies are hostile toward you, but to anyone else too.<br /> Grip of the Damned means a lot of pain for enemies you bite.<br /> Harbringer of the Abyss is good for defending from flames and great for intimidation.<br /> <br /> For a more &quot;good aligned&quot; character:<br /> <br /> Soft Hearted keeps you from straining from the path of virtue.<br /> Life Saver does the work even better, although you'll never be an assassin.<br /> Adolescent or Child might be exploited to appear harmless and / or innocent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27051,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","user":"Solomon Draak","date":". 12-22-2021, 01:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","name":"Solomon Draak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-22T10:17:57-08:00","id":1471092,"title":"","content":"There is a bit of precedent in the wider WoD books for having more than 7 dots of Flaws, if you get them in play (something there's a lot of inconsistency about because the different games have different ideas of what should be a Flaw, and how much they're really something that can happen in play).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-22T13:31:33-08:00","id":1471099,"title":"","content":"Different books treated it a bit differently, some wording it as the limit being a suggestion, other saying that you can take more in Flaws if they are fewer, powerful Flaws, and so on. Being the inconsistent mess they are, character sheets in the many supplements also break that rule with some frequency, so there is precedent. But by V20 RAW, that's that, 7 points.<br /> <br /> But on the Flaws being possibly useful, this is true but not quite. There are many more reasons for those examples of yours to be bad things than just the direct problems you stated.<br /> <br /> As a general rule in VtM, being better at combat does not pay off being worse at not being in a combat to begin with, or with keeping your belly full. Many of those affect directly or indirectly your potential herd, and that limits your feeding options. Others make you better at combat, but also make you more likely to be caught in one to begin with, which is always bad. Withering plants makes it easier for you to move through a forest, but even more so for anyone following you. And Frenzy is always a bad thing because it robs you of agency, so while you may be more dangerous, you're also more stupid.<br /> <br /> More importantly, Flaws are exploitable. You may think of ways to use your flaws on your favor, but your opponents may also learn how to use them against you, and others may have less of a reason to ally with you. It is generally easier to exploit someone's flaws against them than in their favor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-22T15:02:18-08:00","id":1471105,"title":"","content":"It's also, generally speaking, good practice to not allow Flaws to replicate the effects of Merits. If you want a character that's specifically good at coming off as an innocent... there's a Merit for that. Otherwise the Child Flaw shouldn't really give you any greater social advantage that using any other cultural stereotypes in a social setting. A woman vampire with blond hair that plays up the &quot;dumb blonde&quot; tropes to seem harmless and nonthreatening should be looking at basically the same rolling situation as a child vampire trying to play innocent (and remember that vampires very easily give off creepy vibes, and creepy children mess with adult human brains worse than creepy adults because of the association of children with innocence).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-24T20:30:40-08:00","id":1471227,"title":"","content":"Seeing who at the table can make the most unplayably flawed character and then trying to actually play them could make for a funny change-of-pace session. I'd allow it for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}